{% raw %}# Translation style

> **Rules only.** This file is injected verbatim into every translate and audit packet and
> hashed **whole** into the audit context: one changed line marks every finished audit
> `context-changed`. Lists that grow with the chapters (proper names to keep in source form,
> one-word-two-senses registers, chapter-specific usage) belong in `glossary/reference.yaml`,
> where each entry reaches only the packets whose units mention it. Hard, per-unit gates
> belong in `glossary/approved.yaml`. Before editing, ask: did a rule change, or was a record
> added?

- Translate faithfully into clear Simplified Chinese.
- Preserve every {{asset:ID}} reference in its corresponding source block.
- Read original formula and table images in context; do not assume candidates verified.
- Preserve code indentation, citations, numbers, and protected identifiers.
- Keep reader notes separate from translated text.
{% endraw %}